{
  "note": [
    "Listings read by hand from sources that publish no feed and no usable",
    "structured data. Versioned so the work is not lost when the pipeline reruns.",
    "Every field here was read off the organiser's own page — nothing inferred,",
    "nothing guessed. Times and prices come from each event's detail page, not",
    "from the listing index, because the index omits both.",
    "lat/lon may be left null: enrich.py geocodes those from address or",
    "venue + city, which is the one field a person reading a page cannot supply.",
    "Dates were cross-checked against the weekday the source printed beside",
    "them; entries where the two disagreed were dropped rather than guessed at,",
    "as were multi-day runs whose per-day times the page did not spell out.",
    "Remove entries once they have passed; validate.py will not flag them, but",
    "the client hides them and they are dead weight."
  ],
